<title>AUSTRALIA: SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT NEW ZEALAND IN OCEANIA QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AUSTRALIA BEAT NEW ZEALAND IN OCEANIA QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia beat New Zealand 2-0 (halftime 1-0) in the second leg of the World Cup Oceania zone qualifying final on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Ned Zelic 6, Graham Arnold 53.</p>
<p>Attendance: 14,045</p>
<p>Australia won the first leg 3-0 in Auckland on June 28 and win 5-0 on aggregate.</p>
<p>Australia now play whoever comes fourth in the Asian zone preliminary competition with the eventual winner qualifying for the finals in France next year.</p>
</text>
